    {
      "title": "How It Works",
      "content": "The authors introduce the concept of mixed volumes and use it to characterize the vectors of nonnegative real numbers that can arise as the areas of coordinate projections of a convex body in R4. They also provide a proof of Theorem 1.4, which states that a vector p is in \u2206(T2) if and only if there is a convex body A such that p = A ^ A.",
